{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-136824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-3(1)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-3.$ But before we conclude that $-3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-3.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-3(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf6318304e0a6808a0855ad60990c9619c93679873840dc1742a570be74e006c"} {"question" "q-136824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=7{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,7,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf6318304e0a6808a0855ad60990c9619c93679873840dc1742a570be74e006c"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-136826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-4{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf6318304e0a6808a0855ad60990c9619c93679873840dc1742a570be74e006c"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the  maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,2,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf6318304e0a6808a0855ad60990c9619c93679873840dc1742a570be74e006c"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-138075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n6{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{2}^{2},\\,4{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}+6(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bf6318304e0a6808a0855ad60990c9619c93679873840dc1742a570be74e006c"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"} {"question" "q-158533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073873/state.json" "file_sha256" "2dbdb2aca27da87319c5342b7022bc41c5180c29cbd930060b7b7a77f9c3f011"}] "usage" {"q-136824" [] "q-136826" []} "basis" 2711 "retractions" [[17592186167036 :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 2x_{1}^{2} - 3x_{2}^{2} - x_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$."] [17592186167038 :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x) = 7x_{1}^{2} + 8x_{2}^{2} + 5x_{3